From: Kartheek E <karte@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 20 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pwhm: fix BSTA disconnect on BH VAP during FH MLO 11BE->11AX conversion

On MBSS-capable radios (hasMbssidAds=true) getCfgMainVap() always returns
getFirstEnabledVap(), which yields the FH VAP (wlan0.1) because it is the
first entry in pRad->llAP.  Hostapd therefore writes the FH VAP as the
"interface=" (Tx BSS, vdev index 0) and the BH link VAP as the "bss="
(non-Tx BSS, vdev index 1).

If s_doAddLink() finds !hasAvailableCtrlIface but hasReadyGlobalCtrlIface,
the per-BSS sockets have only gone away transiently (reconnecting after the
ath12k cascade).  Proceed with the incremental ADD bss_config via the global
ctrl iface instead of escalating to GEN_FSM_ADD_HOSTAPD, which would
needlessly restart all BSSes on the radio (including any remaining BH VAP).

Signed-off-by: Kartheek E <karte@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
--- a/src/nl80211/wld_rad_hostapd_api.c
+++ b/src/nl80211/wld_rad_hostapd_api.c
@@ -640,7 +640,24 @@ T_AccessPoint* wld_rad_hostapd_getCfgMainVap(T_Radio* pRad)
             pMainAP = wld_rad_getFirstEnabledVap(pRad);
         }
     } else if(wld_rad_hasMbssidAds(pRad)) {
-        pMainAP = wld_rad_getFirstEnabledVap(pRad);
+        /* Prefer a pure-BH VAP as the MBSS Tx BSS (main/first BSS in hostapd config).
+         * When a BH link VAP (wlan0.2) coexists with a FH VAP (wlan0.1) on an MBSS
+         * radio and the FH VAP is the Tx BSS, ath12k cascades vdev/peer teardown to
+         * the BH (non-Tx) BSS when the FH (Tx) BSS vdev is stopped -- e.g. during a
+         * 11BE->11AX conversion (Disable11be=1 on the FH VAP triggers LINK_REMOVE).
+         * Making the BH VAP the Tx BSS avoids this cascade: removing the FH non-Tx
+         * BSS does not force the BH Tx BSS down, so the BSTA stays connected. */
+        T_AccessPoint* pAP = NULL;
+        wld_rad_forEachAp(pAP, pRad) {
+            if(SWL_BIT_IS_ONLY_SET(pAP->multiAPType, MULTIAP_BACKHAUL_BSS) &&
+               wld_ap_isEnabledWithRef(pAP)) {
+                pMainAP = pAP;
+                break;
+            }
+        }
+        if(pMainAP == NULL) {
+            pMainAP = wld_rad_getFirstEnabledVap(pRad);
+        }
     }
     if(pMainAP == NULL) {
         pMainAP = wld_rad_getFirstVap(pRad);

--- a/src/Plugin/wifiGen_fsm.c
+++ b/src/Plugin/wifiGen_fsm.c
@@ -662,13 +662,18 @@ static bool s_doAddLink(T_AccessPoint* pAP, T_Radio* pRad)
         s_schedNextAction(SECDMN_ACTION_OK_NEED_RESTART, pAP, pRad);
     }

     if(!wld_secDmn_hasAvailableCtrlIface(pRad->hostapd)) {
-        SAH_TRACEZ_WARNING(ME, "%s: no conf added yet, falling back to full radio config add", pAP->alias);
-        s_setApplyAction(pRad->fsmRad.FSM_AC_BitActionArray, FSM_BW, GEN_FSM_ADD_HOSTAPD, GEN_FSM_ADD_LINK);
-        s_clearRadLowerApplyActions(pRad, GEN_FSM_ADD_HOSTAPD);
-        s_clearRadDynConfActions(pRad);
-        return true;
+        if(wld_secDmn_hasReadyGlobalCtrlIface(pRad->hostapd)) {
+            SAH_TRACEZ_WARNING(ME, "%s: per-BSS ctrl ifaces not yet available, using global iface for incremental add",
+                               pAP->alias);
+        } else {
+            SAH_TRACEZ_WARNING(ME, "%s: no conf added yet, falling back to full radio config add", pAP->alias);
+            s_setApplyAction(pRad->fsmRad.FSM_AC_BitActionArray, FSM_BW, GEN_FSM_ADD_HOSTAPD, GEN_FSM_ADD_LINK);
+            s_clearRadLowerApplyActions(pRad, GEN_FSM_ADD_HOSTAPD);
+            s_clearRadDynConfActions(pRad);
+            return true;
+        }
     }

     /**
      * Adding an MLO BSS will fail if the primary BSS is non-MLO.
